# Build output. `target` is deliberately unanchored: the fuzz crate is built outside the
# workspace and has a `fuzz/target` of its own.
target
debug

# rustfmt backups
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC debugging information
*.pdb

# cargo-mutants
**/mutants.out*/

# cargo-fuzz working data. The targets are source and are committed; what they find is
# not — the corpus is machine-generated and unbounded, and a crash belongs in `tests/`
# with its input inlined. CI uploads artifacts when a nightly run fails.
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/

# Coverage output, from a local `cargo llvm-cov`.
*.profraw
*.profdata
lcov.info

# macOS
.DS_Store

# RustRover / IntelliJ
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Local research / working notes (not published)
concepts/
specs/

# Zola build output
site/public/
